<title>SRI LANKA: James Finlay 1996 net 92 pct up.</title>
<headline>James Finlay 1996 net 92 pct up.</headline>
<text>
<p>COLOMBO, Feb 5 (reuter) - Unaudited results of James Finlay &amp; Co (Ceylon) Ltd, for the 12 months ended 31 December, 1996.</p>
<p>(in millions of rupees unless stated):</p>
<p>			    1996		 1995</p>
<p>    Turnover	  1,045.90   vs	782.66</p>
<p>    Net profit	   68.14   vs	 35.50</p>
<p>    Tax provision	18.65   vs	  7.36</p>
<p>NOTE - James Finlay, which has owned and managed plantations in Sri Lanka for over 100 years, says in a statement that 1996 was &quot;the best ever in its history&quot;. The good results have been largely due to buoyant tea prices which prevailed thoughout 1996, says the statment.</p>
<p>--Colombo newsroom (941) 434319</p>
</text>
